My name is Kendall Curtis (she/her), and I am an Assistant Professor in the [Department of Political Science](https://olemiss.edu/profiles/klcurti3) at the University of Mississippi. I graduated with my PhD in Government from the University of Texas at Austin in 2025. My research agenda focuses on political parties, legislative institutions, and voter behavior in parliamentary democracies across Europe. I study how the constraints imposed by legislative institutions influence party decisions and color the way voters evaluate parties' brands. My dissertation examines how coalition governance affects voter perceptions of parties and legislative outcomes, including the consequences of coalitions with far-right parties.

I am working on collaborative projects that study how voters perceive early elections and no-confidence motions.
